cartridge "GRAVINAUTS/CLEVELAND M. BLAKEMORE/1985"

' GRAVINAUTS
' A ColecoVision game based on "Gravinauts" by Cleveland M. Blakemore,
' Ahoy! October 1985 (Commodore 64, machine language poked from BASIC
' DATA). Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in
' Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' Not a line-by-line port: the rules are the original's (read from its
' machine code, orig/), the game is built for the ColecoVision: smooth
' sub-pixel flight, drawn glaciers, a rippling acid sea, sound.
'
' The game: on Arkion an acid sea covers everything; gravinauts stay up on
' rocket packs. The button fires your pack (up; with the stick left or
' right, up and sideways); it burns fuel, and gravity pulls you down. Rest
' on the ice glaciers or the launch pad to save fuel. Three rival
' gravinauts chase you: collide with one from above (or level) and its
' pack explodes (250 points); collide from below and yours does. A rival
' that falls into the acid explodes too (250). Fuel tanks stand on the
' glaciers: 5, 10, 15 and 20 units (grey, green, red, gold). When every
' rival is gone and every tank taken, the next wave comes, faster. Touch
' the acid (anywhere but the pad) or run out of fuel: the game is over.
'
' From the original (orig/): one gravinaut, 50 fuel at the start, one unit
' burnt every second thrust step, fuel 0 = your pack explodes; three
' rivals steer toward you (up/down always, sideways on half the steps,
' slower top speed than yours) and never feel gravity; a collision is won
' by the higher one (a tie is yours); rivals in the acid explode; each
' rival 250; four tanks of 5/10/15/20 fuel; the wave ends when all seven
' (three rivals, four tanks) are gone; fuel carries over; each wave is
' faster with a new sky colour; the safe pad in the middle of the sea.
'
' Liberties: smooth motion at 60 steps a second in 1/128 pixels instead
' of the C64's slow whole-pixel steps (thrust three times gravity, a
' little heavier than the C64's four, so you can brake; rivals slower); bounces off ice slide and
' settle (you can stand on a glacier) instead of a random reversal; four
' glacier fields in turn instead of one; the rivals, not you, get faster
' each wave; a rival that lands on ice or hits it from below goes off
' sideways at random (the C64's random bounce); the wall on the right bounces like the left one (the C64
' version wrapped there); a wave banner and a short pause at the start of
' each wave.
'
' Controls (either joystick): the button (either) fires the rocket pack;
' the stick left or right while firing steers. On the title, left and
' right choose START or CREDITS, the button takes it.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table ($702B,
' $7035), effects after; the title tune plays once. `set sprite count`
' after every `clear sprites`. Own xorshift random numbers. Nothing
' flashes: the acid ripples (a pattern shift every 12 frames), the flame
' changes shape every 10 frames.
'
' Workarounds for Amy bugs 37 (u16-small-literal-compare) removed 2026-11-01.

